# .vemo/ holds per-machine runtime state (telemetry, budgets, receipts) — EXCEPT the judge
# provenance log, which is part of the governed record: CI reads it for the required-judge gate,
# and git history is what makes an append-only audit log tamper-evident.
.vemo/*
!.vemo/judge.jsonl
eval/out/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# internal iteration artifacts — not for external deployment
.internal/

# editor / IDE state — never part of the governed surface
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# VEMO_SKILLS is a separate repository (vemodalen-x/VEMO_SKILLS) that is commonly cloned into this
# working tree. Staging it records a bare 160000 gitlink with no .gitmodules, which clones of VEMO
# cannot populate — ignore the path rather than commit a reference that resolves to nothing.
VEMO_SKILLS/
